  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: 'What are GDP and GTP?

'
    basic: "GDP and GTP are small molecules commonly found in cells. \nThey are important
      parts of many cellular processes."
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "GDP and GTP consist of a guanine, a ribose and phosphates. GDP has
      two phosphate groups and GTP has three. \nThey are interconvertible via hydrolysis
      and phosphorylation reactions.eleases energy and becomes GDP.\r"
  - title: 'What function do they serve?

'
    basic: "GDP and GTP  provide energy to various cellular processes. \nThe exchange
      of GDP to GTP completes the activation of the G protein."
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "When GTP is hydrolyzed it releases energy and becomes GDP. \nThis
      energy is harnessed by the cell for various processes. \nIn addition to providing
      energy, GTP and GDP serve unique functions in the cell, including the G protein
      activation cycle and protein syntheses."
